## Q2. Palindrome Number

```javascript
let num = Number(prompt("Enter an integer:"));

let original = num;
let reverse = 0;

while (num > 0) {
    let digit = num % 10;
    reverse = reverse * 10 + digit;
    num = Math.floor(num / 10);
}

if (original === reverse) {
    console.log(original + " is palindrome number.");
} else {
    console.log(original + " is not palindrome number.");
}
```

**Input:**

```text
121
```

**Output:**

```text
121 is palindrome number.
```

