## Q9. Step Number

The absolute difference between every two consecutive digits must be exactly `1`.

```javascript
let num = Number(prompt("Enter a number:"));

let temp = num;
let isStep = true;

while (temp >= 10) {

    let digit1 = temp % 10;
    let digit2 = Math.floor(temp / 10) % 10;

    let difference = Math.abs(digit1 - digit2);

    if (difference !== 1) {
        isStep = false;
        break;
    }

    temp = Math.floor(temp / 10);
}

if (isStep) {
    console.log(num + " is a step number.");
} else {
    console.log(num + " is not a step number.");
}
```

**Input:**

```text
1234
```

Output:

```text
1234 is a step number.
```

